# Hero Mobile Responsiveness To-Do

This file summarizes the changes proposed in `hero-mobile-responsive-plan.md` and how to implement them. Keep this file local: do not add, commit, or push it to GitHub.

## 1. List of all changes

1. Add hero-specific class hooks so responsive fixes do not affect unrelated sections.
2. Split the heading into three intentional lines: “AI Interviews.”, “Better Decisions.”, and “Faster Hiring.”
3. Remove `whitespace-nowrap` from “Better Decisions.” to eliminate the grid min-content overflow.
4. Replace the current discontinuous title sizes with fluid mobile/tablet sizes.
5. Reduce mobile description size, line-height, and spacing while preserving its wording.
6. Use 20px hero/header side padding on mobile and 16px at 375px and below.
7. Add `min-width: 0`, `max-width: 100%`, and `minmax(0, ...)` throughout the hero grid.
8. Render Secure, Reliable, and Smart as one equal three-column mobile chip row.
9. Stack all three mobile CTAs vertically at an equal width capped at 320px.
10. Preserve intrinsic-width CTA wrapping on tablet and desktop.
11. Hide the complete interview mockup below 768px.
12. Show the mockup at 768–1023px, constrained to 620px and centered.
13. Preserve the full two-column mockup at 1024px and above.
14. Reduce the tablet text-to-visual gap to 40px.
15. Keep natural hero height; do not add `100vh`, fixed height, or whole-hero scaling.
16. Compact mobile navbar height, padding, logo, and brand text.
17. Give the hamburger a 44×44px touch target and proper expanded/menu ARIA attributes.
18. Retain and test the tablet header state containing auth buttons plus the hamburger.
19. Reduce the chatbot launcher to 52px on small phones.
20. Use 16px safe-area-aware right/bottom chatbot offsets on small phones.
21. Keep at least 16px horizontal clearance around the open chatbot panel.
22. Run hero pointer tilt only on desktop devices with hover and a fine pointer.
23. Run preview hover transforms only on hover/fine-pointer devices.
24. Keep hero overflow clipping only for decorative glows after real overflow is fixed.
25. Do not add global `body { overflow-x: hidden; }` as a workaround.
26. Preserve colors, copy, labels, logo, desktop visual language, and unrelated sections.
27. Verify all nine required viewports and resize continuously between breakpoints.
28. Run the client build and lint checks after implementation.

